WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.601
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.767
Thank you for being here.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:05.834
That's a crowd.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.968
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:10.367
Well, guys, some good news
for President Biden --

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:12.367
over the past few months,
his approval rating

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:16.067
has gone up by five points,
to 42%.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.234
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:19.734
[ Whistling ]
Biden was like, "Thank God,

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.334
inflation finally got to me."

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:24.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:26.667
Even Biden was surprised
by the results.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.801
He triple-checked it,
like an at-home COVID test.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.868
[ Laughter and applause ]
He's like, "This can't be right.
This can't be right.

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:33.801
Honey, look at this.
Is this right?"

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.868
I'm not even sure
what caused the spike, really.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.868
[ Laughter ]
I mean, apparently,
a lot of Americans thought --

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.300
[ Changes accent ]
Hey, I like how he
handled Easter.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.934
It's great news for Biden,
although it's hard to celebrate

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:45.534
when your approval
rating skyrockets

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:47.467
and it's still only 42%, but.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:48.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.067
Meanwhile,
former President Trump was

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.734
on the campaign trail
this weekend

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:56.000
and, in the Ohio Senate race,
he endorsed J.D. Vance,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.868
who's running against a guy
named Josh Mandel.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.868
I think Trump confused the names

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:03.534
J.D. Vance and Josh Mandel.
Watch this.

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:05.567
-You know,
we've endorsed Dr. Oz.

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:08.534
We've endorsed JP, right?

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.334
J.D. Mandel

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:12.334
[ Laughter ]
and he's doing great.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:13.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:14.868
Not even a person.

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:16.968
[ As Trump ]
Great guy.
JP Morgan is great.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:20.133
You can't say enough
about JCPenney.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.968
[ Laughter and applause ]
I don't think you can.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.334
We love you, J.Lo.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:24.300
We love you.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:28.100
I'm not sure if it's a ringing
endorsement when you're like,

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.534
"I fully support
what's-his-face.

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.534
[ Laughter ]
He's the best."

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:34.000
Trump said even the best leaders
make mistakes sometimes,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.100
like our great president

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.400
AbraGeorge LincolnTon.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.367
Did you guys see this?
Over the weekend,

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:43.534
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
made a surprise visit to Ukraine

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:45.300
and met
with President Zelenskyy.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.868
Here they are together.

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:47.901
Yeah.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:51.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:52.267
Can we see that photo again?

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:54.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.667
Looks like a mom
and her new trainer.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:00.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.634
[ Cheering and whistling ]

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:05.100
Again --
I've said this before.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.767
Why don't politicians
ever know what to do

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:08.133
with their arms in photos?

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:11.567
[ Laughter ]
It's just so bizarre.

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:13.234
Well, the White House
Correspondents Dinner

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:15.334
was on Saturday
and congrats to Trevor Noah

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.167
and President Biden.
They both spoke

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:19.367
[ Cheering and applause ]
and they did a great job.

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:21.868
Very funny, both of them, yep.

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:24.000
The dinner is a tradition
that goes back decades.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.634
In fact, I saw a moment
from one of those early dinners

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.667
that kind of caught me
by surprise. Watch this.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:31.634
-My childhood
in Abilene, Kansas,

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.100
wasn't easy.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.534
I was so ugly,
my mother had morning sickness

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:37.934
after I was born.

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:41.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:44.334
I was so ugly,
my mother used to feed me

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:45.634
with a slingshot.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:49.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:51.133
Now, I drink too much.

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.868
The last time I gave
a urine sample,

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.801
it had an olive in it.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:58.267
[ Laughter and applause ]
Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:00.701
-That's interesting.
I didn't know that.

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:02.167
Have you seen those jokes?

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:03.934
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:06.801
Oh, I read a new report
that said, last year, guys,

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:09.367
the FBI searched
over 3 million Americans'

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:12.200
electronic communications
without a warrant.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.300
[ Oohs, ohs, and booing ]

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.868
People were like, "You can't
invade my privacy like that.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:18.968
But wasn't Becky's text to me
like super weird?

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:21.334
[ Laughter ]
I mean, it was --

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.834
There was a tone, right?
There was a tone?"

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.701
[ Laughter ]
Yep, after reading

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.734
3 million texts and emails,
the FBI learned

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:28.567
that the only thing harder
than planning an attack

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:29.934
is planning brunch.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:31.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:32.667
"I can't make it that weekend."

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.767
Some business news --
Spirit Airlines

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.400
has rejected JetBlue's offer
to buy them

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.901
and will merge
with Frontier Airlines, instead.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:44.701
[ Oohs ]
-What?

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:49.000
-That's crazy. Picking Frontier
over JetBlue is like

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.100
deciding to fly Frontier
over JetBlue,

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.300
[ Laughter and applause ]
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.634
Imagine getting turned down
by Spirit Airlines?

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:57.601 --> 00:03:58.767
It's like getting
a rejection letter

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:00.234
from the University of Phoenix.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:01.334
You go like, "Come on."

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:03.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:06.434
[ Cheering ]

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.968
Get this --
I heard that inflation

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:13.934
is causing the cost of summer
camps to drastically increase.

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:15.234
Yeah, right now,
a lot of parents

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:16.734
are looking
at the high prices like,

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:18.601
"Camp iPad it is.
Here we go."

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:20.400
[ Laughter and applause ]
And finally, this is cool --

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.534
over the weekend, at a track
meet in Philadelphia,

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:26.334
a 100-year-old man
ran the 100-meter dash.

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:28.200
-Whoo!
-It's exciting, although,
when he started the race,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.667
he was 98.
-Oh.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:34.067
Sadly, he was disqualified
after testing positive

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:35.300
for every medication.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.267
But what a moment.
After he finished,

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.501
his friends dumped a cooler
of Ensure over his head.

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:43.133
[ Laughter and applause ]
It was a great moment
and congratulations to him.

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:45.467
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

